{{/*
  PP-034 — this file used to define `slack.nucrm.url` and `webhook.nucrm.url`, built like:

      {{- if env "SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL" | not -}}{{- $url = env "SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL" -}}{{- end -}}

  Two independent reasons that never could have worked, both measured rather than assumed:

  1. The condition is inverted — it assigns the variable only when it is empty.
  2. `env` is not a function in Alertmanager's template funcmap. Proof:

       amtool check-config <config that lists this file under `templates:`>
       FAILED: template: default.tmpl:7: function "env" not defined

  ...so adding a `templates:` key that references this file would make alertmanager refuse to
  load its config, not start with empty URLs. `amtool check-config alertmanager.yml` currently
  reports `0 templates`: this file is mounted at /etc/alertmanager/templates but never read,
  and neither define was referenced anywhere.

  Both defines are therefore deleted rather than fixed. A webhook URL belongs in
  alertmanager.yml (`webhook_configs.url`), which compose cannot interpolate at that level;
  if Slack is ever wired here, the URL has to come from the config file itself (rendered by
  the deploy pipeline) or from a receiver integration — not from a template expression.

  Keep this file comment-only unless `templates:` is added to alertmanager.yml AND something
  here actually formats a message; re-run `amtool check-config` either way.
*/}}
